<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Lemnos</h1><p class="st-meta">1207 CE – 1278 CE (approx.) · capital Myrina</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Venetian family lordship on the northern Aegean island of Lemnos after the Fourth Crusade, whose lords bore the title of megadux of the Latin Empire.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1207 the Venetian noble <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/filocalo-navigajoso">Filocalo Navigajoso</a> seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lemnos">Lemnos</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> as part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> carve-up of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a>. The Latin emperor named him megadux, grand duke, giving him a high rank in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/latin-empire">Latin Empire</a>, and his heirs kept both title and island.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of how the Navigajoso governed. They held the island as a hereditary fief, collecting revenues from a Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> population of farmers and herders, and depended on their link to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/latin-empire">Latin Empire</a> for support. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lemnos">Lemnos</a> was valued for its grain and its position near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellespont">Dardanelles</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> recaptured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in 1261, the island was exposed. The admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/licario">Licario</a>, serving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-viii-palaiologos">Michael VIII Palaiologos</a>, besieged the Navigajoso and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lemnos">Lemnos</a> around 1278, returning it to Byzantine rule.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1207 CE – 1278 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Greece and the Aegean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:83.72%;width:1.41%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1207 CE – 1278 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Myrina</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Filocalo Navigajoso</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity (rulers), Eastern Orthodox Christianity (population)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Italian, Medieval Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Megadukes of Lemnos</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1242&amp;focus=lordship-of-lemnos" aria-label="Lordship of Lemnos on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5297 751 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Lemnos lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5617 1007L5709 970M5617 1007L5709 970"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5617 1007h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5617 1007h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Myrina. <a href="/atlas?year=1242&amp;focus=lordship-of-lemnos">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

